oic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":1.0,"_gp_incr_roic":true,"_score_incr_roic":100.0,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.05794977962992012,"_gp_margin_advantage":true,"_score_margin_advantage":52.6,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":-0.005905212294226803,"_gp_margins":false,"_score_margins":44.1,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.10083458372485282,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":100.0,"_gate_share_shrink":null,"_gp_share_shrink":null,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.09406734366648851,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.11007,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":73.4,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Maplebear Inc., doing business as Instacart, operates as a technology and enablement partner for the grocery industry in the United States and internationally. The company offers Instacart Marketplace which helps retailers serve customers' needs by supporting fulfillment options, shopping occasions, and categories; Instacart Enterprise platform, an end-to-end technology solution for retailers across all aspects of business; and Instacart Ads, enables brands to learn more about general consumer behavior from discovery to purchase, offering insights about how to optimize advertising spend. It also provides advertising solutions, including sponsored product ads, display ads, coupons, and brand pages; and software-as-a-service. The company's services can be provided through company's mobile application or website. Maplebear Inc., was incorporated in 2012 and is headquartered in San Francisco, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Chris  Rogers | Chairman, CEO & President | Age 46 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 3K people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the top quartile among Consumer Cyclical peers, improving at 11%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $253K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $98K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 1\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Maplebear Inc. is a large-cap consumer cyclical business with a $13.7B market cap on $3.7B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +11% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +41.9pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 23% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 13-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat. Gross margins of 75% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $910M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 24 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 2.17\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -14.2% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Management returns a meaningful 10.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and within its sector the business captures 1.6\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Very elevated short interest (15.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Carries a 71% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.7104765336456174},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $18.3M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Cyclical sectors like Consumer Cyclical tend to underperform in slowdowns","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Consumer staples outperforming discretionary, signaling cautious spending","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Gross margin tops the Consumer Cyclical peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Maplebear (NASDAQ:CART) Price Target Raised to $65.00","source":"thelinco